<!--
  ats_invalid_negative_line_amount.xml — a per-line amount is negative.

  Rule exercised: monedaType, ats.xsd:1304-1310. minInclusive 0.0 at
  ats.xsd:1306 forbids a negative value, and the pattern at ats.xsd:1308
  ("[0-9]{1,12}\.[0-9]{2}|[0-9]{1,12}") has no negative alternative either, so
  the document is rejected twice over.

  Element under test: detalleCompras/montoIva, ats.xsd:745.
  Every monedaType field of detalleComprasType (ats.xsd:740-762) behaves this
  way: baseNoGraIva, baseImponible, baseImpGrav, baseImpExe, montoIce, montoIva,
  valRetBien10, valRetServ20, valorRetBienes, valRetServ50, valorRetServicios,
  valRetServ100, valorRetencionNc and totbasesImpReemb.

  Consequence for the builder: a credit note is reduced by emitting a positive
  line amount; it can never be expressed by negating a line. Compare
  ats_invalid_negative_total_ventas.xml, where the aggregate does admit "-".
-->
